{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4","id":461996,"title":"Claws of the Unholy + Protean 4","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T01:11:29-07:00","id":461996,"title":"Claws of the Unholy + Protean 4","content":"So taking a read of the Claws of the Unholy merit, I'm wondering if by the Rules As Written it means that once you have the merit you can't change your Unnatural Aspect to anything else because it states that the claws automatically pop when you're in frenzy and that it's not optional? Or is it that your current Unnatural Aspect gets thrown over for claws whenever you frenzy and would that stay in place for the rest of the night? Or is it that Claws of the Unholy are only a factor when you have the claws set?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:18:34-07:00","id":462015,"title":"","content":"Am too curious about this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","name":"Azerkatil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:20:26-07:00","id":462019,"title":"","content":"Well, this hasn't been discussed and I guess you have to make the decision for your own table.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I like all the options and I'm not even sure... Locking the user into using Claws is kidna limiting the power a lot (a lot more than the things it provides), so I'd probably go with either option two (upon frenzy your chosen Aspect switches), or with option 3... <br /> <br /> <br /> But I dislike option 3, due to how much easier the drawback is to fight, so... Uh... I vote option 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:49:40-07:00","id":462139,"title":"","content":"I'd vote option 2, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:56:04-07:00","id":462144,"title":"","content":"I would go option three, it is a Merit not a Flaw. Yes it has drawbacks. No, the drawback is not the main point. You want uber-claws in frenzy, be sure to have that Aspect. You don't want to? Easy, just have another Unnatural Aspect on. Is not like they were permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:00:50-07:00","id":462147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4?p=462019#post462019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dislike option 3, due to how much easier the drawback is to fight</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the alternate drawback of potentially not having them available at all when you need them is enough to offset that. <br /> <br /> Think about it, if you put them away it's like you never bought the merit at all. No benefit, no drawback. Seems fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:59:53-07:00","id":462206,"title":"","content":"I am in the camp that they can switch Aspects, then lose access to Claws of the Unholy, but regain it once they change back to Horrid Talons. Trying to use the ability to switch Aspects to circumvent the downside of the Merit (potentially overkilling someone) requires a degree of foresight, which makes it okay in my book. Also, it costs an extra investment of precious Life.<br /> <br /> Also, should the vampire's Beast change to a new form (as implied in the Gangrel writeup) which would make Horrid Talons unfitting in general, I would have Sanctitiy of Merits apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:58:02-07:00","id":462703,"title":"","content":"Two valid interpretations depending on which line you emphasize.<br /> <br /> &quot;When wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect while in frenzy, this Merit takes effect.&quot; Therefore, if you are not wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect while in frenzy, there is no effect.<br /> <b>Or</b><br /> &quot;Once purchased, this modification is not optional; the character manifests Claws of the Unholy any time she\u2019s frenzied.&quot; Therefore, the character gains Claws of the Unholy on top of any modification she currently has. If you stand by this, it's also reasonable to assume that the cost is free and the transformation is automatic, since they'd manifest even if you are at 0 Vitae.<br /> <br /> I proffer emphasis the first line for one simple reason: the second says that she manifests &quot;Claws of the Unholy&quot; (which in turn brings us back to referencing the first line) and it does <i>not</i> say that you automatically use or manifest Unnatural Aspect. Therefore the merit is automatically in play, but as long as you are not &quot;wielding claws borne of Unnatural Aspect&quot; then the merit has no effect. This also means that if you frenzy and do not whip out your horrid talons for some reason (your goal is to have sex with someone instead of murder them, or you're running away and too busy spending your blood on Celerity, for instance) the merit's drawback does not apply. However, although I say that, keep in mind that the beast is in control during a frenzy and &quot;I don't want to brutalize them with obvious agg damage&quot; isn't a particularly valid argument for not using Horrid Talons if that is the best and most immediate option available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T16:01:32-07:00","id":462762,"title":"","content":"I'd say you can have the +0 agg claws if you want them. If you don't than you don't have to. But, if you frenzy then they always pop out, even you didn't currently have claws as an assigned aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:18:17-07:00","id":463198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4?p=462762#post462762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say you can have the +0 agg claws if you want them. If you don't than you don't have to. But, if you frenzy then they always pop out, even you didn't currently have claws as an assigned aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No you can't just decide that your claws are agg. You must go frenzy if you want agg (Ride the wave)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:53:03-07:00","id":463697,"title":"","content":"If you've got a form with claws, Claws of the Unholy kicks in. If you avoid a form with claws, it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T04:52:33-07:00","id":1103445,"title":"","content":"Sorry for digging up the old topic. I know there are already a few topics about claws of the unholy and swarm form, but I just realised that Rose answered that questions as well in this topic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4?p=463697#post463697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've got a form with claws, Claws of the Unholy kicks in. If you avoid a form with claws, it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it mean that a swarm form with claws can use claws of the unholy? Or the damage is always lethal, due to merit description. What do you think?<br /> I have a feeling that by RAW it works fine, since for example in frenzy you must manifest them even in bat or rat swarm form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T05:41:44-07:00","id":1103450,"title":"","content":"That sounds scary and unnatural and is therefore a good fit with Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T11:23:36-07:00","id":1103555,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure the standard interpretation is that yes, Swarm Form can manifest Predatory and Unnatural Aspects, including Claws of the Unholy, just like any other Beast's Skin form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:25:42-07:00","id":1103618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4?p=1103445#post1103445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for digging up the old topic. I know there are already a few topics about claws of the unholy and swarm form, but I just realised that Rose answered that questions as well in this topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does it mean that a swarm form with claws can use claws of the unholy? Or the damage is always lethal, due to merit description. What do you think?<br /> I have a feeling that by RAW it works fine, since for example in frenzy you must manifest them even in bat or rat swarm form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to reread Swarm Form (my group's gangrel has it but hasn't used it so far) but sounds pretty cool and horrific to me, therefore very fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T01:11:54-07:00","id":1103748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/461996-claws-of-the-unholy-protean-4?p=1103555#post1103555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pretty sure the standard interpretation is that yes, Swarm Form can manifest Predatory and Unnatural Aspects, including Claws of the Unholy, just like any other Beast's Skin form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same feeling, just was curious what more experienced players or developers say. If someone doesn't like it, he or she can ban it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}